<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Tally — iOS entitlements.

  TRIMMED 10 Aug 2026. PWABuilder generated this file with two problems that
  would have failed code signing:

  1. macOS App Sandbox keys in an iOS app — com.apple.security.app-sandbox,
     .device.camera, .device.audio-input, .files.user-selected.read-write,
     .network.client, .personal-information.location, .print. These are macOS
     entitlements. iOS apps are sandboxed implicitly and never declare them;
     an App Store provisioning profile does not include them, so signing fails
     on an entitlement mismatch. All removed.

  2. com.apple.developer.associated-domains pointing at applinks/webcredentials
     for tallytracker.github.io — the host RETIRED on 28 Jul 2026. Two separate
     problems: the host is dead, AND the App ID (io.github.tallytracker.tally)
     has Sign in with Apple and Push Notifications enabled but NOT Associated
     Domains, so requesting the entitlement fails signing outright. Tally does
     not use universal links or password autofill, so it was removed rather
     than repointed. If it is ever wanted, enable the Associated Domains
     capability on the App ID first and use tally-app-c82c6.web.app.

  WHAT REMAINS: aps-environment only. Push Notifications IS enabled on the App
  ID, and the app uses Firebase Cloud Messaging, so this one is both correct
  and required. "production" is right for App Store and TestFlight builds.

  ADDED 11 Aug 2026 — com.apple.developer.applesignin. Required for the NATIVE
  Sign in with Apple sheet (Face ID, no password). Without it,
  ASAuthorizationController fails at runtime with error 1000.

  This one is safe to request, unlike the associated-domains entitlement
  removed above: Sign in with Apple IS already enabled on the App ID
  (io.github.tallytracker.tally), as the note above records, so the App Store
  provisioning profile includes it and signing succeeds.

  WHY IT WAS NEEDED: the web fallback (appleid.apple.com inside the webview)
  cannot reach the device keychain, so it demands the Apple ID password and its
  passkey button does nothing in a WKWebView. Almost nobody remembers that
  password now that Face ID exists, which made Apple sign-in present but
  effectively unusable. Guideline 4.8 does not require the native sheet, so
  this is a conversion fix rather than a compliance one.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>production</string>
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
